===Serbia vs Switzerland===
{{further|List of 2018 FIFA World Cup controversies#Swiss celebrations against Serbia}}
[[File:Swiss fans Russia 2018.jpg|thumb|right|Swiss players and fans celebrating Shaqiri's goal]]
The two teams had never met. Playing as [[Yugoslavia national football team|Yugoslavia]], the two teams met 13 times, including one game at the [[1950 FIFA World Cup]] group stage, a [[1950 FIFA World Cup Group 1#Yugoslavia vs Switzerland|3–0]] victory for Yugoslavia.<ref name=Kit11/>

[[Dušan Tadić]] checked back onto his left foot to send in a cross from the right that [[Aleksandar Mitrović (footballer)|Aleksandar Mitrović]] met with a header into the left side of the net. [[Blerim Džemaili]] shot wide from inside the penalty area. Serbia pressed and [[Sergej Milinković-Savić]] shot narrowly wide with a rising 20-yard drive. With almost half an hour played [[Steven Zuber]] passed the ball to Džemaili who drew a one-handed save from [[Vladimir Stojković]] down to the goalkeeper's right. After 52 minutes, [[Xherdan Shaqiri]]'s shot rebounded back to [[Granit Xhaka]] and the midfielder curled a right-footed shot into the far corner of the net from 25 yards. Shaqiri hit the frame of the goal with a bending effort from the right. Switzerland substitute [[Mario Gavranović]] was flagged offside as he hit the side-netting. And, in the final minute of normal time, Gavranović played a throughball to Shaqiri, who outpaced [[Duško Tošić]] and ran from near the half-way line into the box before nutmegging Stojković with a low finish from the left.<ref>{{cite web |last=Henry |first=Matthew |title=Serbia 1 Switzerland 2 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44439145 |work=BBC Sport |date=22 June 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Creek |first=Stephen |title=Shaqiri strikes late to clinch crucial comeback victory |url=http://www.goal.com/en-om/match/serbia-v-switzerland/report/2ziirq41dmiglgulpqxztlq7d |website=Goal.com |date=22 June 2018}}</ref>

[[Stephan Lichtsteiner]] made his ninth World Cup appearance for Switzerland in this game, breaking the national record held by [[Charles Antenen]] since 1962.<ref name="SRB-SUI recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/shaqiri-stuns-serbia-to-give-swiss-hope |title=Shaqiri stuns Serbia to give Swiss hope |publisher=FIFA |date=22 June 2018 |access-date=22 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520045950/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/shaqiri-stuns-serbia-to-give-swiss-hope |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref>

